{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778992289345,"sessionID":"ses_1cbcde07effeAvXdikQzO7zQh7","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_NtTbIBlIUATVb7POmjjmfmq8","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+Addressed in PR #<NN>.\n+\n+Updated `CL_0001057` and `CL_0001058` to add CD14-negative to both the textual definitions and logical axioms, with the requested OMIP references added to the definition xrefs. I did not change `CL_0001056` because the issue discussion noted that the broader human dendritic cell term should remain unchanged due to known CD14-positive human dendritic cell populations.\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n+Implemented the requested hierarchy/definition update for the two specific human dendritic cell terms discussed in issue #3163.\n+\n+Changes made:\n+- Updated `CL_0001057` (`myeloid dendritic cell, human`) to state that it is `CD14-negative` in the textual definition.\n+- Updated `CL_0001058` (`plasmacytoid dendritic cell, human`) to state that it is `CD14-negative` in the textual definition.\n+- Added `lacks_plasma_membrane_part some PR_000001889` to the logical axioms for both terms, using the existing CL pattern for negative surface marker representation.\n+- Added the requested OMIP references as definition xrefs: `PMID:34260151`, `PMID:36470845`, `PMID:37254600`, `PMID:38343094`, and `PMID:40095400`.\n+- Left `CL_0001056` (`dendritic cell, human`) unchanged, consistent with the issue discussion noting that the broader human dendritic cell class should not generally be constrained as CD14-negative.\n+\n+Rationale:\n+- The issue requested the CD14-negative phenotype for the specific human myeloid and plasmacytoid dendritic cell terms.\n+- The local ontology already models negative marker phenotypes with `CL_4030046` (`lacks_plasma_membrane_part`), so I followed that existing pattern rather than introducing a new modeling approach.\n+- The cited OMIP papers support use of CD14-negative gating to distinguish these dendritic cell populations from monocytes in human immunophenotyping workflows.\n+\n+Validation performed:\n+- Confirmed the existing term blocks and nearby modeling patterns in `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl`.\n+- Resolved the CD14 protein identifier from existing ontology usage (`PR_000001889`).\n+- Ran `robot convert --input src/ontology/cl-edit.owl --output /tmp/opencode/cl-edit-3163.ofn` to parse-check the edited ontology successfully.\n+\n+Completed checklist:\n+- [x] Read imported issue context\n+- [x] Verified scope from issue discussion\n+- [x] Updated only `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl`\n+- [x] Added requested references without removing existing ones\n+- [x] Kept `CL_0001056` unchanged\n+- [x] Validated ontology parses after edit\n+- [x] Committed only the ontology file\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\nA PR_COMMENTS.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+++ /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@\n+Addressed in PR #<NN>.\n+\n+Updated `CL_0001057` and `CL_0001058` to add CD14-negative to both the textual definitions and logical axioms, with the requested OMIP references added to the definition xrefs. I did not change `CL_0001056` because the issue discussion noted that the broader human dendritic cell term should remain unchanged due to known CD14-positive human dendritic cell populations.\n\nIndex: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n+++ /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@\n+Implement